According to passage [1], if an Authorised Person fails to comply with Rule A4.3.18, it must:

(a) inform the Regulator as soon as practicable;
(b) assess the effect of the situation in terms of the risk posed to the Authorised Person;
(c) prepare a plan to rectify the situation and inform the Regulator of its plan as soon as practicable; and
(d) undertake prompt corrective action within a reasonable time in accordance with the plan prepared pursuant to (c).

This is the standard procedure for an Authorised Person to rectify the situation and avoid revocation of its approval.

According to [1] (30) CONCEPTS RELATING TO THE DISCLOSURE OF MINING ACTIVITIES, a Mining Reporting Entity (including a Petroleum Reporting Entity) should consider factors such as:

d) whether its actual and projected revenue from the Mining Project is, or is likely to be, material in the context of its revenue from other Mining Projects and other (non-Mining) business activities;

e) whether it considers the Mining Project will be a material asset in the medium to long term;

When assessing the importance of a project's projected revenue, a Petroleum Reporting Entity should consider these factors to determine if the disclosure of information about the project is material.
